{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8946-1",
  "summary": "unbound vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled certain TCP connections.\nA remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Unbound to consume\nresources, leading to a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu\n26.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-80225)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled certain DNS responses. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to crash Unbound, resulting\nin a denial of service. (CVE-2026-81634)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled certain DNS responses\nduring DNSSEC validation. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause Unbound to consume resources, leading to a denial of service.\n(CVE-2026-85501)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled outgoing network ports.\nA remote attacker could possibly use this issue to crash Unbound, resulting\nin a denial of service. (CVE-2026-50252)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled certain DNSCrypt\npackets. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to crash Unbound,\nresulting in a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 26.04\nLTS, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS, Ubuntu 20.04 LTS and Ubuntu 18.04\nLTS. (CVE-2026-40691)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled certain cached DNS\nresponses. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to poison\nUnbound's cache. This issue only affected Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, Ubuntu 24.04\nLTS, Ubuntu 22.04 LTS and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-44690)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled certain DNS-over-QUIC\nconnections. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nUnbound to consume resources, leading to a denial of service. This issue\nonly affected Ubuntu 26.04 LTS. (CVE-2026-32665)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled certain EDNS options. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to crash Unbound, resulting\nin a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 26.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2026-55973)\n\nElias Heftrig, Haya Schulmann, Niklas Vogel, and Michael Waidner discovered\nthat Unbound incorrectly handled validating DNSSEC messages. A remote\nattacker could possibly use this issue to cause Unbound to consume\nresources, leading to a denial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu\n18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 16.04 LTS and Ubuntu 14.04 LTS. (CVE-2023-50387)\n\nIt was discovered that Unbound incorrectly handled preparing an NSEC3\nclosest encloser proof. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause Unbound to consume resources, leading to a denial of service. This\nissue only affected Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, Ubuntu 16.04 LTS and Ubuntu 14.04\nLTS. (CVE-2023-50868)",
